sections/abstract.tex:10:The one positive statement is narrow: calcite is thermodynamically suitable against dissolution (a necessary condition) for calcite in \NumRegSlurryPassCalcite\ of \NumRegSlurryCellsCalcite\ cells of the processing grid, at total calcium \NumRegWindowLoCalcite\ to \NumRegWindowHiCalcite\ and pH \NumRegSlurryPhLow\ to \NumRegSlurryPhHigh; it is not evidence of protection.
sections/abstract.tex:12:If the screen's model holds, then in slurry immersion and anodic holds in a fluorine-free electrolyte a calcite film stays undissolved and unoxidised at low voltage, hydroxyapatite is thermodynamically excluded at the high hold, and condensed or aluminium phosphate films are not excluded there.%
sections/design.tex:68:Three in-situ routes try to outrun that hydrolysis: gelation of a soluble polyphosphate at the oxide by the aluminium ions released there; a calcium polyphosphate coacervate, a dense liquid phase that separates from solution\cite{wang2024liquidliquid}, which wets the foil and dries to a glass; and calcium polyphosphate trapped by fast drying. % CL-D13
sections/design.tex:80:Here $k_\mathrm{eff}$ is the rate constant measured on alumina particles at room temperature\cite{wan2019polyphosphate} times a transfer factor to the process state, bracketed from both sides. % CL-D14
sections/discussion.tex:9:The positive statement is the dissolution label of calcite at the alkaline processing stage, over the passing cells named in Section~\ref{sec:res-dissolution}; it is a necessary condition only, and the screen gives no evidence that any film forms on the foil, that a film keeps the slurry off the metal, or that layers build up. % CL-S17, CL-D20
sections/discussion.tex:31:The contrary records point the same way as the exclusions rather than against them: calcite scale on aluminium alloys was porous with attack beneath it\cite{osoriocelestino2020influence}, and a polydopamine coating reduced carbonate deposition\cite{yu2023study}; neither tests a templated film, and both are weighed, not set aside. % CL-L05, CL-E01, CL-E02
sections/discussion.tex:35:Phosphoric-acid pH control enters as the comparator state of the dissolution test, in which calcite dissolves at the lower pH values and the apatites pass only at high dose at the lowest pH, and carbon-coated foil and the two patent baselines enter only through their rows. % CL-L08, CL-S08, CL-S11
sections/introduction.tex:10:Water-processed lithium-ion cathodes replace the fluorinated binder and organic solvent with fluorine-free binders cast from water\cite{heidbuchel2022enabling}. % CL-K01
sections/introduction.tex:11:Lithium leaching from the active particles then drives the slurry strongly alkaline\cite{hawley2020lithium,bauer2019effects}, and at that pH the native \ce{Al2O3}/\ce{AlOOH} film on the aluminium collector converts to hydroxide and dissolves, exposing the metal during slurry contact\cite{heidbuchel2022enabling,li2016effect,doberdo2014enabling}. % CL-K02, CL-K03
sections/introduction.tex:16:Phosphoric acid added to the slurry lowers its pH and so avoids corrosion of the aluminium collector\cite{chen2024study,carvalho2016study}, at the price of careful control of stoichiometry and drying against reactive phosphate residues\cite{tolchard2023insights}, and a carbon-coated collector keeps the slurry off the metal\cite{bichon2021performance}. % CL-V05, CL-V06
sections/introduction.tex:20:On steel, films grow in situ from dosed polyphosphate and polyvalent cations, while the polyphosphate hydrolyses to orthophosphate in competition\cite{morsch2018unexpected}. % CL-V10
sections/introduction.tex:24:Nacre is aragonite platelets in an organic matrix of proteins and chitin\cite{sedira2026nacre,osunamascaro2015ultrastructure}, grown through amorphous calcium carbonate precursors observed at its growth front\cite{devol2015nanoscale,gong2012phase}; chitosan, the partly deacetylated derivative of chitin\cite{younes2015chitin}, is the processable form used here. % CL-K12, CL-K06
sections/introduction.tex:25:In zebrafish fin bone, mineral arrives as amorphous calcium phosphate that transforms into apatite in the collagen matrix\cite{mahamid2010mapping}. % CL-K13
sections/introduction.tex:27:The screen does not test layered architecture or polymorph structure, and alternating aragonite and calcite layers are not nacre-like. % CL-L10
sections/introduction.tex:39:In the cell, oxidation releases its calcium and lattice oxygen, and calcium carbonate is thermodynamically excluded\footnote{\label{fn:excluded}\NumExcludedNote.} above about \NumCarbonateCrossover; lithium carbonate is observed to oxidise close to the equilibrium limit of the same reaction\cite{mahne2018electrochemical,cao2022oxidative}. % CL-S02, CL-R13
sections/introduction.tex:40:Aragonite, the polymorph of nacre, is not reported to form from solution at slurry pH and room temperature; it needs magnesium, a polyamine or heating\cite{nahi2022polyamines,hanifa2025effects}. % CL-K15
sections/introduction.tex:41:Calcite scale on aluminium alloys was porous with attack beneath it\cite{osoriocelestino2020influence}, and a polydopamine coating reduced carbonate deposition\cite{yu2023study}. % CL-E01, CL-E02
sections/methods.tex:41:Supersaturations (Eq.~\eqref{eq:stability}) follow from measured solubility products and the slurry speciation, and the passivation window of aluminium comes from our own Al--O--H Pourbaix construction on benchmarked ion data\cite{persson2012prediction}, governed by amorphous \ce{Al(OH)3}, the least ordered hydroxide and the one expected on the foil in water at room temperature, with boehmite as the reference and both published windows beside them\cite{tolchard2023insights,kuhnel2016water}. % CL-D05, CL-M13
sections/methods.tex:77:Monte Carlo draws from the joint prior, with copula rank correlations, are propagated through the relations of Section~\ref{sec:design}; Sobol indices rank independent inputs\cite{saltelli2002making,archer1997sensitivity} and Shapley effects correlated ones\cite{iooss2017shapley}, with draws sized by a rule on the half-widths of the band masses (\nacreSIref{si:methods}{Methods detail and the carbonate control}). % CL-M03
sections/methods.tex:82:Solid-phase energies were taken from the Materials Project\cite{jain2013commentary} (database version \NumMpDatabaseVersion\ for the carbonate control and \NumMpDatabaseVersionComparator\ for every database comparator column), used under the Creative Commons Attribution \NumMpLicenceVersion\ International licence (CC~BY~\NumMpLicenceVersion, \url{https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/}); entries derived from GNoME, licensed CC~BY-NC, were excluded. % CL-M06, CL-M16
sections/methods.tex:94:An earlier rough estimate under the calcite framing was available when the project was designed, and the framings were chosen on literature grounds (\nacreSIref{si:methods}{Methods detail and the carbonate control}). % CL-M08
sections/predictions.tex:12:If the screen's model holds, then a calcite film stays undissolved in the model slurry inside the passing region of Section~\ref{sec:res-dissolution} and dissolves at the low-dose corner, and it is not oxidised at the \NumClassLo\ hold, below the measured onset of lithium carbonate at \NumTierTwoLow; it is thermodynamically excluded\nacreExcludedMark\ above about \NumCarbonateCrossover, so at the higher hold it is expected to lose calcium with release of carbon dioxide. % CL-Q05
sections/results.tex:26:Calcite is thermodynamically suitable against dissolution (a necessary condition) for calcite in \NumRegSlurryPassCalcite\ of the \NumRegSlurryCellsCalcite\ cells of the processing grid, at $\mathrm{Ca_T}$ \NumRegWindowLoCalcite\ to \NumRegWindowHiCalcite\ and pH \NumRegSlurryPhLow\ to \NumRegSlurryPhHigh; the grid carries no phosphate, and the phosphate rows assume $\mathrm{P_T}$ on the same decade grid, \NumRegWindowPLo\ to \NumRegWindowPHi, because no slurry phosphate total is sourced. % CL-S17
sections/results.tex:28:Aragonite passes in \NumRegSlurryPassAragonite\ cells, at $\mathrm{Ca_T}$ \NumRegWindowLoAragonite\ to \NumRegWindowHiAragonite, as dissolution stability only, because its formation is unsupported at slurry pH and room temperature\cite{nahi2022polyamines,hanifa2025effects}. % CL-S17, CL-K15
sections/results.tex:30:Alternating aragonite and calcite layers would not be nacre-like, and the screen tests neither layering nor polymorph structure. % CL-L10
sections/results.tex:37:Calcite dissolves at every cell below pH \NumRegAcidFirstCalcite\ and passes in \NumRegAcidPassCalcite\ of \NumRegAcidCellsCalcite\ cells above it, so the incumbent state and the carbonate route are chemically opposed. % CL-S08
sections/results.tex:49:Lithium carbonate is measured to oxidise at \NumTierTwoLow\ to \NumTierTwoHigh, at the equilibrium limit of the same reaction\cite{mahne2018electrochemical,cao2022oxidative}, so the carbonate claim is worded as low voltage up to about \NumTierTwoLow. % CL-S15
sections/results.tex:64:  \caption{Stability map of the slurry-stage phases against the cutoff classes. (a) One row per phase at its oxidation upper bound (solid-salt sink): calcite, $\alpha$-TCP, amorphous calcium phosphate, $\beta$-TCP, hydroxyapatite and brushite; circle area is the passing fraction of the acid-adjusted dissolution test, filled where the lowest passing dose is below \NumRegHighDose; crosses are thermodynamically excluded\nacreExcludedMark, plus signs open, dots undetermined. (b) Bars from the upper bound; the lower end is pending for every row. Grey bands: the cutoff classes. Octacalcium phosphate, \ce{Li3PO4}, \ce{Al(PO3)3} and the Al gel (\NumRegNoKOneBound\ phases) are omitted from the stability map because no $K_1$ bound exists for them.}
sections/results.tex:95:The registered ignorance prior puts \NumNucMassSourced\ of its mass there under the sourced calcite $\gamma_\mathrm{nv}$, and at most \NumNucMassDesignMax\ over the design points with enough admitted draws, whatever $\gamma_\mathrm{nv}$ (its support widens with $\gamma_\mathrm{nv}$). % CL-T03
si/main_si.tex:103:Three in-situ routes try to outrun that hydrolysis: gelation of a soluble polyphosphate at the oxide by the aluminium ions released there; a calcium polyphosphate coacervate, a dense liquid phase that separates from solution\cite{wang2024liquidliquid}, which wets the foil and dries to a glass; and calcium polyphosphate trapped by fast drying, which has no formation criterion of its own and is decided by hydrolysis and the amorphous onset alone. % CL-D13
si/main_si.tex:104:Here $t_\mathrm{wet}$ runs from mixing to the end of drying, and $k_\mathrm{eff}$ is the rate constant measured on alumina particles at room temperature\cite{wan2019polyphosphate} times a transfer factor to the process state, bracketed from both sides. % CL-D14
si/main_si.tex:118:A literature row is admitted for an input only if it measures the quantity the input defines, under its conditions or under conditions stated as different; a proxy, a different quantity used in its place, is never admitted, and rows that cite one original determination count once. % CL-M01
si/main_si.tex:124:Where measured analogs exist, such as the contact energy of a different organic template against calcite, the analog prior runs side by side with the ignorance prior, flagged, and its verdict is stated as conditional on the analog. % CL-M02
si/main_si.tex:130:Main-effect and total-order Sobol indices with bootstrap confidence intervals rank the independent inputs\cite{saltelli2002making,archer1997sensitivity}, and Shapley effects, which share variance among correlated inputs without assuming independence, rank them where a correlation group is active\cite{iooss2017shapley}; the Shapley ranking is repeated under independence as a check. % CL-M03
si/main_si.tex:145:Calcite and amorphous calcium carbonate are both framings, and each is run as a whole chain with its own solubility product, molar volume and nucleus--liquid energy, never mixed across links; the verdict is falsified only if the study is falsified under every framing and feasible if it is feasible under at least one, which is then named with the other beside it, while the dissolution test uses the calcite solubility product under both. % CL-M05
si/main_si.tex:161:Dissolution (\Rs) & $\Omb\ge1$ & the driving force of nucleation; calcite solubility product\\
si/main_si.tex:183:Solid-phase energies were taken from the Materials Project\cite{jain2013commentary} (database version \NumMpDatabaseVersion), retrieved through its interface and used under the Creative Commons Attribution \NumMpLicenceVersion\ International licence (CC~BY~\NumMpLicenceVersion, \url{https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/}). % CL-M06
si/main_si.tex:185:We modified the data as follows: the \NumMpCorrectionScheme\ compatibility corrections and the aqueous-compatibility adjustments were applied; the Pourbaix entries were rebuilt offline from the solid entries and the aqueous ion reference data following the scheme of Persson and co-workers\cite{persson2012prediction}; amorphous calcium carbonate was represented as calcite plus a literature free-energy offset; and for the lithium-referenced window an all-experimental thermochemical route replaced the computed energies where experimental data exist, with the computed gas-reference schemes reported as benchmarked comparators. % CL-M06
si/main_si.tex:187:The slurry construction holds carbon in the carbonate system at the regime dissolved inorganic carbon, removes the dissolved calcium species from the hull because dissolution is the $\Omb$ test, and evaluates the worst point of the specified pH and potential region against a tolerance from the formation-energy error of the database\cite{stevanovic2012correcting,wang2021framework}; a construction that allows carbon redox is a labelled sensitivity. % CL-M06
si/main_si.tex:190:The all-experimental route uses tabulated thermochemistry for every reactant and product\cite{rossini1971selected,rossini1981selected}\nacreMissing{reference for the NIST-JANAF tables, whose DOI the bibliography tool could not resolve}, and its margin $m_\mathrm{expt}$ combines the tabulated uncertainties per transferred electron with a bound on the neglected solid entropy of \ce{Ca(ClO4)2} taken from analog salts. % CL-M06
si/main_si.tex:197:Its level was chosen from published benchmarks for \ce{Ca^2+} with oxygen-donor ligands rather than copied from a periodic set-up: the \NumAnchorFunctional\ functional, which had the lowest error among the functionals benchmarked against coupled-cluster references for \ce{Ca^2+} binding by carboxylate-type ligands\cite{friedman2021preferential}, with the all-electron \NumAnchorBasis\ basis and \NumAnchorDispersion\ dispersion\cite{goerigk2017look}, and the SMD continuum model for water\cite{marenich2009universal}, whose non-electrostatic term a run must include or record as omitted. % CL-M07
si/main_si.tex:198:Geometries, conformers and thermal corrections come from \NumAnchorGeometryMethod\ with implicit water and a conformer search\cite{bannwarth2019gfn2,ehlert2021robust,pracht2020automated}. % CL-M07
si/main_si.tex:206:An earlier rough estimate under the calcite framing was available when the project was designed, and it lay near the shape-factor edge of the nucleation criterion that was set later; the framings were chosen on literature grounds, calcite as the stable polymorph and the amorphous phase as the precursor seen at the growth front of nacre\cite{devol2015nanoscale}, and both are run as whole chains so that the verdict does not depend on a framing chosen after that estimate. % CL-M08
